# Two applications that call the SDK, for Phase 5.3.
#
# Two, not one, and that is the point. Each gets its own scope — its own keys,
# under app/<namespace>/<app>/ — so the walk can give them different secrets and
# then have one reach for the other's. Until ADR 0018 decision 5 that reach
# succeeded, and the 5.3 walk recorded it succeeding, because every application
# in an instance shared one storage scope and the keyholder's data path
# authenticated only the server. It is now refused twice over: beta's key space
# is not addressable with alpha's leaf, and not openable with alpha's keys.
# A fixture with a single application could only ever show the happy path.
#
# Neither declares an external host: the only thing this fixture talks to is
# the in-cluster keyholder, which the translated NetworkPolicy already allows.
#
# The code lives in the SDK module (sdk/go/examples/demo) so the build context
# is that module and nothing has to be downloaded to compile it. Paths are
# repository-relative, as they are in every manifest.
#
# The top-level name is the namespace, so these applications are addressed
# sdk-demo/alpha and sdk-demo/beta — and 'farcast run --namespace' overrides it,
# which is how a walk mints a fresh set of scopes without editing this file.
name: sdk-demo
apps:
  - name: alpha
    containerfile: sdk/go/examples/demo/Containerfile
    context: sdk/go
  - name: beta
    containerfile: sdk/go/examples/demo/Containerfile
    context: sdk/go
